# v0.32 W1: the unit suite READS files out of this repo — MANUAL.md, the `claude-jam` launcher,
# every module (three lints scan their string literals) and the `capture-pane` corpus. A Windows
# checkout with git's default `core.autocrlf=true` would hand those files back with `\r\n`, and a
# lint that matches a line ending would fail on Windows for a reason that has nothing to do with
# Windows. LF everywhere, in the working tree as well as in the object store.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The pane fixtures are VERBATIM terminal captures — ANSI, box drawing, cursor moves. They are
# the corpus the frame parsers are tested against, so not one byte of them may be normalised by
# anybody, on any platform.
fixtures/pane/*.txt -text
